# Tank Board II (003112) -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Tank is two boards with no CPU. MAME's netlist (nl_tank.cpp) describes both as one circuit
# at the pin level, on one grid of designators -- but the boards each have their own grid,
# so Board I's D11 is not Board II's D11. This file is the part of MAME's circuit the sheets
# put on Board II, with every net that crosses to the other board landing on the cable
# contact Board II's sheet prints for it (Board I J1/J2 to Board II J4/J5).
#
# MAME's passive designators carry suffixes it added to tell the boards apart (R53A, R48B,
# C33C, R4V, R102MX, R74M1); they are stripped here, so the designators are the sheet's.
# Where a part's board was in doubt, the sheets decided: MAME's "A" mostly means Board I's
# sheet 2, but R8A-R11A and R37A are Board II's.
#
# Board II: ROM multiplexing, playfield, minefield, the motion latches, the motor sounds and
# video (sheet 1); sync, timing and control (sheet 2).
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/atari/nl_tank.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(tank). Licence BSD-3-Clause by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Ryan Holtz (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/atari/nl_tank.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 434: dropped NET_C(CLK.Q, IC_A7.1, IC_A7.3) -- an ideal 14.318 MHz clock; the crystal oscillator is put back
# line 852: dropped NET_C(IC_D11.12, IC_E11.1) -- Board II sheet 2: D11 QA (12) clocks E11 pin 14, not pin 1
# line 853: dropped NET_C(IC_D11.11, IC_E11.14) -- Board II sheet 2: D11 QD (11) clocks E11 pin 1, not pin 14
# line 1001: dropped NET_C(GND, IC_R10.9) -- Board II sheet 1 takes K10 pin 9 to -12V
# line 1019: dropped NET_C(GND, IC_N13.7, R19.2, R20.2, R21.2, R22.2, R23.2, R24.2, R25.2, R26.2) -- took R19.2, R20.2, R21.2, R22.2, R23.2, R24.2, R25.2, R26.2 out of it: Board II sheet 1 pulls the ROM outputs to -12V, not ground
# line 1826: dropped NET_C(ATTRACT, IC_N13.1) -- Board II's ATTRACT is its own M13.2 (from /ATTRACT); MAME takes Board I's
# line 1865: dropped NET_C(ATTRACT, IC_N13.13) -- as above
# line 1888: NET_C(GND, IC_E8.1, IC_E8.2) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1889: NET_C(GND, IC_E13.1) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1890: NET_C(GND, IC_A7.5, IC_A7.9, IC_A7.11, IC_A7.13) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1891: NET_C(GND, IC_J14.14) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1892: NET_C(GND, IC_E12.3, IC_E12.4, IC_E12.5, IC_E12.6) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1893: NET_C(GND, IC_D12.3, IC_D12.4, IC_D12.5, IC_D12.6) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1894: NET_C(GND, IC_N7.11, IC_N7.12) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1895: NET_C(GND, IC_B7.12, IC_B7.13) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1896: NET_C(GND, IC_D7.5, IC_D7.6, IC_D7.8, IC_D7.9) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1897: NET_C(GND, IC_L14.14) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1898: NET_C(GND, IC_A14.1, IC_A14.2, IC_A14.13) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1899: NET_C(GND, IC_B10.13) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1900: NET_C(GND, IC_D11V.1, IC_D11V.3, IC_D11V.5, IC_D11V.11, IC_D11V.13) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1902: NET_C(GND, IC_L11.13, IC_L11.14) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1903: NET_C(VCC, IC_L11.15) -> nc -- tied to +5V in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1907: NET_C(GND, IC_J7.5, IC_J7.6) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1908: NET_C(GND, IC_F13.1, IC_F13.2) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1909: NET_C(VCC, IC_J11.9, IC_J11.11, IC_J11.13) -> nc -- tied to +5V in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1890: MAME ties UA7.11, UA7.13 off as unused, but the circuit uses them -- the tie is dropped
# line 1900: MAME ties UJ11.1, UJ11.3, UJ11.5 off as unused, but the circuit uses them -- the tie is dropped
# line 1901: MAME ties UM13.3 off as unused, but the circuit uses them -- the tie is dropped
# line 1909: MAME ties UJ11.9 off as unused, but the circuit uses them -- the tie is dropped
# line 1911: MAME ties UN13.1, UN13.13 off as unused, but the circuit uses them -- the tie is dropped
# lines 1797-1833: restored from a comment -- the Motor 1 sound, which MAME comments out; compared with Board II sheet 1 and corrected below
# lines 1837-1872: restored from a comment -- the Motor 2 sound, likewise
# Declarations MAME comments out but the restored circuit uses, restored: C43 (line 172), C44 (line 173), C47 (line 174), C48 (line 175), C49 (line 176), C50 (line 177), C51 (line 178), C52 (line 179), C53 (line 180), C54 (line 181), C55 (line 182), C56 (line 183), CR13 (line 224), CR14 (line 225), VR2 (line 192), VR3 (line 193), VR4 (line 194), VR5 (line 195), Q27 (line 235), Q28 (line 236), Q29 (line 237), Q30 (line 238), Q31 (line 239), Q32 (line 240), Q33 (line 241), Q34 (line 242), R100 (line 116), R101 (line 117), R102 (line 118), R103 (line 119), R35 (line 60), R36 (line 61), R64 (line 93), R65 (line 94), R66 (line 95), R67 (line 96), R68 (line 97), R69 (line 99), R70 (line 101), R71 (line 103), R72 (line 105), R73 (line 107), R74 (line 108), R75 (line 109), R76 (line 110), R77 (line 111), R78 (line 112), R79 (line 113), R80 (line 114), R81 (line 115)
#
# Corrected from the sheet (the notes below say what was read where):
#   UN15: the sheet's part is MFC6040, MAME's MC3340 -- Board II sheet 1 prints MFC6040; pins mapped as for K6
#   UF15: the sheet's part is MFC6040, MAME's MC3340 -- Board II sheet 1 prints MFC6040; pins mapped as for K6
#   UA7: the sheet's part is 74H04, MAME's 7404 -- Board II sheet 2 prints H04 -- it is the crystal oscillator
#   UK10: the sheet's part is EA-ROM, MAME's MK28000 -- Board II sheet 1 prints '24-PIN EA ROM' at K10, no part number; MAME's MK28000 is a substitute (see the notes)
#   C51: the sheet's value is 0.22uF, MAME's 22uF -- Board II sheet 1 prints .22uf at C51
#   C50: the sheet's value is 0.22uF, MAME's 22uF -- Board II sheet 1 prints .22uf at C50
#   parts the sheet draws that MAME does not have: R1 330, R2 330, R12 680, C1 0.1uF, Y1 14.318MHz, C29 10uF
#   Board II sheet 2: START in from J5-15 to M13 pin 3: UM13.3
#   Board II sheet 2: /START is M13 pin 4: UM13.4 (STARTQ)
#   Board II sheet 1: the motor sounds' ATTRACT is M13 pin 2: UM13.2 UN13.1 UN13.13
#   Board II sheet 2: the 14.318 MHz crystal oscillator, which MAME replaces with an ideal clock: UA7.13 R2.1 R12.1 Y1.1; UA7.12 R2.2 C1.1 UA7.1 UA7.3; C1.2 UA7.11 R1.1; UA7.10 R1.2 Y1.2; R12.2
#   Board II sheet 2: D11 QA clocks E11 CPA: UD11.12 UE11.14 (SCR1E)
#   Board II sheet 2: D11 QD clocks E11 CPB: UD11.11 UE11.1
#   Board II sheet 1: HD1 from N8 Q-bar: UN8.6 (HD1)
#   Board II sheet 1: HD2 from N12 Q-bar: UN12.6 (HD2)
#   Board II sheet 1: K10 pin 9 and the output pull-downs on -12V: UK10.9 R19.2 R20.2 R21.2 R22.2 R23.2 R24.2 R25.2 R26.2
#   Board II sheet 1: the summed video through C29: R3.2 C29.1
#   Board II sheet 1: C29 to J6-21: C29.2 (VIDEO_OUT)
#   Board II sheet 1: Q34's emitter on +12V, which MAME's commented-out block omits: Q34.E
# line 1093: RVID is not a part -- MAME's 10K to ground standing in for the monitor's input
# line 1830: R555OUT1 is not a part -- a 1K to ground on the 555's output, which the sheet leaves undrawn
# line 1869: R555OUT2 is not a part -- a 1K to ground on the 555's output, which the sheet leaves undrawn
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): SWITCH(P1_LEFT_UP), SWITCH(P1_LEFT_DOWN), SWITCH(P1_RIGHT_UP), SWITCH(P1_RIGHT_DOWN), SWITCH(P1_FIRE), SWITCH(P2_LEFT_UP), SWITCH(P2_LEFT_DOWN), SWITCH(P2_RIGHT_UP), SWITCH(P2_RIGHT_DOWN), SWITCH(P2_FIRE), SWITCH2(COIN1), SWITCH2(COIN2), CLOCK(CLK), CLOCK(NOISE_CLOCK)
#
# Left out by MAME (commented out at TAG, so not in this file either):
#   line 158: CAP(C34A, CAP_U(0.01)) Decoupling
#   line 1090: RES(RPROBE, 220)
#
# Compared with both Board II sheets in full (003112 sheet 1 rev H, sheet 2 rev F),
# 2026-10-19. MAME agrees with the sheet on the ROM's address and data wiring and the 74153
# and 9322 multiplexers, the playfield shift register, the minefield and mine control (the
# 8277 included), video summing, the boom and shot one-shots, the motion latches apart from
# HD1/HD2, the joystick and fire inputs (designators and values once MAME's suffixes are
# dropped), the shell one-shots, the 556 blow-up timer, the speed and rotation counters, and
# the 7492 at A12 -- which matters because MAME's own 7492 model swaps QB and QD against TI's
# data sheet (the MiSTer Tank core's finding); the netlist's pin numbers are the sheet's.
#
# MAME's errors here, all corrected above: the score counters (D11 QA and QD go to E11's CPA
# and CPB the other way round, and SCR1E is D11 pin 12, not 11 -- MAME has SCR1E and SCR2C on
# one pin); HD1 and HD2 are the Q-bar outputs of N8 and N12 (pin 6), not Q; the ROM's pin 9
# and its output pull-downs R19-R26 go to -12V, not ground; and C50/C51 are .22uF, not 22uF.
# MAME's ideal clock is replaced by the crystal oscillator the sheet draws on A7 (a 74H04);
# its "unused" A7 pins 11 and 13 are the oscillator. The motor sounds, which MAME comments
# out, are restored: its block agrees with the sheet apart from the MFC6040's output and
# supply pins, C50/C51 and Q34's emitter (missing from MAME's +12V list), all corrected; the
# 555s' pin 3 is not drawn.
#
# The ROM. The sheet prints "24-PIN EA ROM" at K10 -- an Electronic Arrays MOS ROM, with +5V
# on pin 1 and -12V on pin 9. MAME models it as an MK28000 bipolar PROM, and a handwritten
# note on the rev F print points to the MK28000P; an MK28000's pin 9 is GND, so the board as
# drawn is not wired for one. The pin names here are MAME's MK28000 names, which are what
# MAME's ROM dump is ordered by. R19-R26 have no value printed; MAME's 1K is its own guess.
#
# Open questions, each as printed and not settled:
# * The cable's VLD1 and /FIRE1 contacts disagree with Board I's sheet (see Board I's notes).
# * J5-22/23 is labelled -12V beside the ROM and +12V in the regulator.
# * R13 (PLAYFIELD SELECT, 4.7K to +5V) has a jumper to ground drawn beside it -- the
#   alternate maze. MAME leaves it open, as this file does.
# * R74 reads 120K on rev H and 180K on rev F; MAME and this file have 180K.
# * A8's first half has its S and R pins marked "R" rather than "P".
# * Player 1's lower stick pair is printed "#2 LEFT STICK" -- it feeds ACC1/STOP1/RR1/RL1.
# * 1Ø2-1Ø4 and 2Ø2-2Ø4 reach this board in contact boxes with no number printed.
#
# Designators that are not MAME's: J11 (MAME's "D11V" -- another gate of J11), K10 (MAME's
# "R10"), R18 (MAME's "RUNK1", 47K). Ours, not printed: Y1 (the crystal), VR1 (the 50K shell
# range pot, circled 'Shell Range' by hand on the sheet), VR2-VR5 (the motor volume pots and
# rheostats). Not in this file: the +5V regulator (Q35-Q39 and its parts), not in MAME.

